  "contract": "Classify escaped Markdown highlight delimiters according to backslash parity without changing note source: odd-length runs leave the delimiter literal and allow normal Markdown rendering; even-length runs retain active syntax and visible source fallback.",
  "implementation": {
    "document_layer": "crates/doc counts a contiguous backslash run before a highlight opener. For an odd run it skips the first escaped equals sign before scanning for active highlight markers; for an even run it scans the opener normally.",
    "fixture_and_docs": "The shared dialect fixture covers odd and even escape parity. The inventory SHA-256 and native Markdown preview architecture documentation were updated.",
    "source_integrity": "Markdown analysis is read-only and does not normalize or mutate the source. Existing unescaped highlight syntax remains source-only."
  },
  "focused_tests": {
    "command": "cargo test --workspace --locked (GitHub Actions only)",
